  "period_note": "CONSOLIDATED (Group) basis, matching this bank's main Q4/annual series (see sources.json reporting_basis). Source: Southeast Bank's own BSEC-mandated 'Evaluation of the Quarterly Financials by the Audit Committee and by the Board' disclosure table, embedded in its annual report (a corporate-governance disclosure most banks answer with a checkbox, but which Southeast Bank answers with an actual Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 balance-sheet-and-income-statement table for that report's own year, plus a comparative column for the prior year). Balance-sheet line items are the 1 January to 30 September 2022 period-end snapshot (basis reported). Income-statement line items and EPS are CUMULATIVE FROM 1 JANUARY 2022 (\"1 January to 30 September 2022\" exactly as the table's own column header states), not discrete-quarter figures -- flagged via the _cumulative suffix, basis reported, same convention as CITYBANK. Balance-sheet identity (Total assets = Total liabilities + Total equity + Non-controlling interest) holds to within BDT 1m rounding. Cumulative net profit after tax increases monotonically Q1->Q2->Q3 within 2022 (validated; no violation). Cross-checked against the FY2023 report's comparative column: Q1, Q2 and Q3 match exactly. Q4's 'Profit before provision (C=A-B)' subtotal is printed as 10,303m in the FY2022 report's own table, which does not equal its own Total operating income (17,587m) minus Total operating expenses (7,157m) = 10,430m; the FY2023 report's comparative correctly shows 10,430m. This is confined to that one intermediate subtotal -- Q4 net profit after tax (1,752m) is identical in both reports -- and does not affect this file (Q4 is not included here). NOTABLE FINDING: the same Q4 pattern recurs again: cumulative net profit fell from 3,439m (9-month) to 1,752m (full year), with cumulative provision for loans rising from 2,905m (9-month) to 6,593m (full year), a roughly 3,688m Q4-alone provisioning charge. Flagged in insights.json.",
